# Double remainder by zero is rejected

Takes 10.5 modulo zero to verify a zero divisor fails with a
language-level division-by-zero error instead of producing a value.

>>> source
const dividend: double = 10.5
const divisor: double = 0

const remainder: double = dividend % divisor
print(remainder)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: division by zero

<<< exit
1
